  "idea": "A studio's red light meant the microphone was live: a WEEI studio sign photographed in Boston warns that silence is required while the red light is on, and Australia's national sound archive keeps a 1940 lightbox lit for the same reason. Here red is kept for the one thing that is live (Play, and what is playing), and the blue of 1930s mirrored-glass sets carries everything else you can touch.",
