  "idea": "From 1935, RCA's 6E5 tuning eye glowed green behind the dial, its dark wedge closing as a station came in, and Bakelite cabinets came out brown or black because the wood-flour filler that made them strong hid any lighter dye. Green means tuned in (Play, progress, the selected tab), on a near-neutral ground with walnut brown for the mark.",
