  "idea": "Catalin was cast without filler, so late-1930s sets came in butterscotch, oxblood, and marbled onyx, and collectors note that red, black, and maroon kept their color while lighter shades yellowed toward butterscotch. Oxblood leads in light mode and butterscotch in dark, the pairing of a 1939 DeWald set in butterscotch with oxblood trim.",
